  "how_it_is_actually_run": "the engine couples exactly two period matrices on a common random field per sample, so a family is two paired runs on disjoint seed streams rather than one three-orientation run. Differencing within a pair kills C; two pairs determine A4 and A8; the third pair is their exact sum and is a check, not a third run. See paired_difference_plan on each family",
